1478123],"toleranceM":0.75,"sourceZoom":15},"osm":{"type":"relation","id":3344870,"version":43,"timestamp":"2025-08-30T17:57:02Z","url":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/relation/3344870"},"additionalOsm":[],"rightsStatus":"approved","geometryStatus":"approved","attribution":"Open Landmarks; contains © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL-1.0","references":[{"title":"File:Paris Sainte Chapelle East View 02.JPG","author":"Uoaei1","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","sourcePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paris_Sainte_Chapelle_East_View_02.JPG","sourceSha1":"ff212b66f8e6338dc0561508ff3582ddd8bee4e5","use":"visual-reference-only","view":"Modern east oblique: apse, roof, buttress rhythm and spire; no sculpture reproduction."}],"aliases":[],"authors":["Open Landmarks contributors"],"artisticLicense":"CC-BY-4.0","spatialDataLicense":"ODbL-1.0","licenseScope":"CC BY applies to original artistic contributions only; ODbL applies to OSM-derived spatial data. Reference photographs retain their own licenses.","assistance":"AI-assisted architectural interpretation and procedural recipe authoring; deterministic Python/Blender export. No photographic textures.","review":{"status":"approved","revision":"b5fbbc03ef8d9d02b012f17a03566496fcb067bfe53d8dcc3ca60bd63cf33ce3","reviewer":"Benjamin TD","reviewedAt":"2026-09-30","checks":{"rights":"passed","footprint":"passed","appearance":"passed","mapIntegration":"passed"}},"modelingNotes":["Plan (OSM, bundled): chapel body relation/3344874 (30 m walls), 14 buttress parts relation/3344873 (35 m with 5 m pinnacles), roof parts way/248296374 + way/248296313 (eaves 30 m, ridge 42 m, half-cone over the apse), west turrets way/248296385 + way/248296384 (36 m shafts, spirelets to 46 m), facade pinnacles relation/3344875 (31/38 m), two-storey porch relation/3344872 (15 m) with five 18 m buttress pinnacles relation/3344871, flèche way/265389509 + way/248296312 (47-75 m) with eight 52 m corner pinnacles. Total height 75 m kept.","Bays come from the mapped wall facets between buttresses: 4 nave bays per side + 7 apse bays = 15 upper windows (matches the 15 windows of the upper chapel). Nave windows get 4 lights (two pairs, two small and one large oculus), apse windows 2 lights and an oculus.","Researched dimensions (Wikipedia / Monuments nationaux): ridge ~42.5 m, spire 75 m (Lassus 1853), upper windows ~15.5 m tall, lower chapel ~6.6 m, west rose ~9 m wide (flamboyant, c.1490). Used: upper windows 10.0-25.6 m, lower chapel windows 2.6-7.2 m, floor string course 8.4 m, cornice 29.3 m, openwork balustrade 30-31.1 m, window gables (wimpergs) 26.1-31.5 m, rose Ø 7.6 m centred at 22.4 m in a pointed arch.","Inferred: porch storey levels (lower arcade to ~7 m, upper porch openings 8.2-13.4 m, terrace balustrade to 15 m, central upper gable to 17.3 m), the west gable with a small rose and crown of thorns, the lantern stage of the turrets (33-36 m), the flèche stages (openwork lancet stage 43-50.6 m, lattice needle with eight ribs, rings and a gilded fleur-de-lys crown) and the gilded ridge cresting and apse angel.","Simplified: tracery is rayonnant-schematic (no cusps), rose tracery is a flamboyant-like petal pattern, sculpture, gargoyles and crockets are omitted; the footprint pieces joining the Palais de Justice are kept as the 25 cm foundation only."],"source":{"url":"/objects/949b760b3b9b0fafe83ff3c15b744d41918769b366bd5a07c5c468376c9a2d58/source.blend.gz","bytes":528474,"sha256":"949b760b3b9b0fafe83ff3c15b744d41918769b366bd5a07c5c468376c9a2d58"},"spatialSource":{"url":"/objects/0d691d05f0b89c8a0c57d96cbfe3f2623fb4aa47dac161debe74f2c400caf794/spatial-source.json","bytes":23830,"sha256":"0d691d05f0b89c8a0c57d96cbfe3f2623fb4aa47dac161debe74f2c400caf794"},"preview":{"url":"/objects/1d0cabdb285c8ffa9d2df42e8fec1b84d9a0becab7c920e65569271d563ac998/preview.webp","bytes":11414,"sha256":"1d0cabdb285c8ffa9d2df42e8fec1b84d9a0becab7c920e65569271d563ac998"},"previewDi